{"_id":"6a2ff5fb2204ffbc59e5a68d","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"yRHodYYqdICLZyG3J9qjc","description":"# Pandas String Methods\n\nPandas exposes string methods through the `.str` accessor on Series, allowing vectorized text operations on entire columns. Methods include `.str.strip()`, `.str.lower()`, `.str.contains()`, `.str.replace()`, `.str.split()`, and `.str.extract()`. These methods avoid the need to loop over rows for string cleaning.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Working with text data","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/user_guide/text.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeba0"},{"type":"article","title":"5 Must-Know Pandas Operations on Strings","url":"https://towardsdatascience.com/5-must-know-pandas-operations-on-strings-4f88ca6b8e25/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeba1"},{"type":"video","title":"How do I use string methods in pandas?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bofaC0IckHo","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeba2"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:54:19.800Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/yRHodYYqdICLZyG3J9qjc.md"}